-- V1.9.4 — Programmation multi-semaines (25 November 2026). A coach prepares a cycle of several weeks, adapts it for one athlete, sends it
-- once, sees which sessions were accepted, and revises one occurrence, one week or the rest of the cycle without losing what was accepted.
-- Behind the server flag screens.coach_programs (absent = closed). It REUSES what exists and copies nothing private:
--   the sharing link (public.coach_links: scope, pause of capacity, revocation) decides every read and every write, at that moment;
--   every session of a sent programme is an ordinary public.coach_assignments row (status proposed): the athlete answers it in their own
--   space exactly as before (portal, V1.9.1 follow-up, Android « Mes suivis de coaching »), links it to a journal session through the same
--   session_id, and it shows in the coach's queue (V1.9.1) and weekly review (V1.9.3) like any proposal;
--   the V1.9.1 rules of a change: a session already accepted (or declined) is never overwritten by a revision — the change waits beside the
--   version in force (pending_change, accepted_version kept) until the athlete accepts it; a session done and linked is never touched;
--   the V1.9.1 projection of a linked session (private.titan_coach_followup_row): outside the link's contract the coach reads « liée » only.
-- New:
--   private.titan_coach_programs / _program_versions  the coach's multi-week templates (« modèles »), versioned: saving creates a new
--                     version, the older ones stay readable, a programme keeps the version it came from;
--   private.titan_coach_plans  a programme adapted for one link (« duplication par sportif »): a draft the athlete never sees, its preview
--                     against its starting point, then sent once (state sent), then closed;
--   private.titan_coach_plan_versions  one immutable entry per send, revision and closing, with what was decided and a snapshot of every
--                     session (no measure): the weeks already played keep their versions;
--   public.coach_assignments.plan_id, plan_key, plan_week  the session of the programme a proposal comes from (unique per programme: a
--                     replayed send never creates a second proposal), discuss_note, discuss_at  « à discuter » asked by the athlete.
-- A revision is previewed first (dry_run) and applied only with the preview's key: if anything moved meanwhile (an answer, a link) the
-- application is refused (COACH_CONFLICT). A revision carries an op_id: replaying it returns the version it created and writes nothing.
-- private.titan_coach_followup_row is re-applied with two additive changes: the state « to_discuss » (a proposal the athlete wants to
-- discuss: a case for the coach in the queue and the weekly review) and the programme a proposal belongs to.
-- No action writes public.training_logs, a note or a check-in. No XP, no credit, no notification. Additive. The caller owns the
-- transaction: never BEGIN/COMMIT here.
